162-/**
163- * Run a build's parts in order so each part can only ADD to what earlier parts built: a write into a cell an earlier
164- * part placed (air included, so no carving) is refused, counted, never thrown, so a later part can't knock holes in
165- * a wall. Cells set before runParts (the ground) stay writable: farmland and paths may replace grass. With a palette
166- * (palette.json, or its object: { roles: { role: [blocks] }, objects: [blocks] }), every block placed outside it is
167- * reported. Prints one line per part, writes the reports to `report` (default parts-report.json; null for none) and
168- * returns them.
169- *   runParts(g, [["shell", shell.build], ["garden", garden.build]], { palette: "palette.json" })
170- */
